<node id="11149075" title="Re^2: Number too big to fit in integer" created="2022-12-25 02:53:12" updated="2022-12-25 02:53:12" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;That's tricky: for a number that doesn't fit in UV (integer), Perl automatically stores it in NV (double) which can result in an immediate loss of precision.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[id://11108835|See also] [https://github.com/Perl/perl5/blob/v5.36.0/Porting/Glossary#L4523|&lt;c&gt;$Config{nv_overflows_integers_at}&lt;/c&gt;]:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
$ uname -p
x86_64
$ perl -MConfig -le 'print eval $Config{nv_overflows_integers_at}'
9007199254740992
&lt;/c&gt;</doctext>
